    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d798">

                <pb facs="0898" n="1732" xml:id="pg1732"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.711/18</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gonzales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-09T11:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 9, 1918, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11.45 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mine, March 6, 12 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d798-f1"/> Two steamships from Spain
                    being due today, one bound for Mexico, I urged upon President that pending
                    general action upon censorship this mail for Mexico be examined. He has just
                    replied: “I took up matter with Spanish Minister and it has been settled in
                    accordance with your wishes.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
